**Croesus.** Spell so; see ^^Æ^^, ^^Œ^^.
>>>

<<<
cromorne, krummhorn, cremona. Either the first or the second should be used, the second being the original (German), the first the French pronunciation of the second, & the third a misleading confusion with Cremona (violin &c.).
===
**cromorne, krummhorn, cremona.** Either the first or the second should be used, the second being the original (German), the first the French pronunciation of the second, & the third a misleading confusion with *Cremona* (*violin* &c.).
>>>

<<<
 crooked. See -ER & -EST, 2. A stick that is not straight is a kroo‘kid stick; one provided with a crook is a krookt stick. croquet.
===


**crooked.** See ^^-ER^^ & ^^-EST^^, 2. A stick that is not straight is a kroo͝o'kĭd stick; one provided with a crook is a kroo͝okt stick.

**croquet.**
>>>

<<<
 For -ed, -ing, sec CROCHET, crosier, -zier.
